Subject: Name the copies of host-visible memory and log their totals

The copies the driver keeps of an app's host-visible memory are anonymous mappings, so dumpsys
meminfo counted them under "Unknown" with everything nobody named, and nothing said how much of
an app's memory they were. Each copy's mapping is now named [anon:dsa-vk-copy]
(dsa_driver_memory.h), so smaps and meminfo list them per app.

The driver also counts, for its process, the live copies and grants of the graphics memory the
host shares, and why each copied allocation was not granted: no shared memory, kept out by the
host, or not mapped by the kernel. mapSharedMemory says which. When an allocation is made or
freed and three minutes have passed since the last, one line with those totals goes to the log.

